      "problem": "Evaluate $\\sqrt{3x-1}$ for $x=3.$",
      "worked_solution": "We replace $x$ with $3$ in the given expression, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3x-1} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{3\\cdot 3-1} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{9-1} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{8} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify even further using the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{8} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{4\\cdot 2} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{{2}^{2}\\cdot 2} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{{2}^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{2} & = \\\\ 2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
